note.text:
Mixtures are named by the states of their parts:
• solid–solid: sand and salt; garri with small stones;
• solid–liquid: muddy water, salt water;
• liquid–liquid: palm oil and water (they do not mix: immiscible); ethanol and water (they mix: miscible);
• gas–liquid: a soft drink (carbon dioxide dissolved in water);
• gas–gas: air;
• solid–gas: smoke.
A solution is a mixture where a solid, liquid or gas (the solute) dissolves completely in a liquid (the solvent): salt water. A suspension has solid pieces that do not dissolve and settle on standing: muddy water.
